{"number":1550,"title":"Self-test gate passes a `--root` flag `selftest.mjs` never parses","body":"`runSelfTest` invokes the vendored self-test with `--root  --strict` (`packs/claudinite-lifecycle/updates/engine-update.mjs:94`), but the self-test CLI never reads `--root` — it resolves its root as `process.env.CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR || process.cwd()` (`engine/selftest.mjs:257`). Only the spawn&#39;s `cwd: root` keeps the gate honest, and only while `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` is unset in the caller&#39;s environment.

Anywhere `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` is set and differs from the gated checkout (the corpus&#39;s own spawn rule expects the precedence `--root`, then `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`, then `cwd`), the gate silently judges the wrong tree — a wrong verdict in either direction. Whether any live caller hits the mismatch today is unconfirmed (worker contexts appear to coincide); the dead flag is verified either way. Fix is one line: parse `--root` in the CLI, ahead of the env fallback.

